window.docContents[239].resolve({"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L2-___-The-pair-is-a-system-too--Synopsis--PKC-vocabulary-in-scope":{"contents":"New at this step:\n\n* Composite (whole, part) — the object type of a whole and its parts.* Decomposition (atom, union) — how a whole is carved into parts.* Assembles — the aggregation licence, keyed by the sort of the whole and the kind.* assemble — fold a licensed quantity over a decomposition.* Extensive — a kind whose value over a union is the sum over its parts.* DedicatedKind, KindOfProperty.dedicatedTo — a kind dedicated to one sort, such as the pair's normal-mode frequency.* Component — a named component of a system's characterization.* displacementK — spring extension; negative compressed, positive stretched.\n\nCarried from earlier steps: IndividualQuantity, IndividualQuantity.add, DifferenceKind.ofScale, SortOfSystem, Sorted, Designated, massK, springConstantK.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Onboarding: Human Context Protocols\u0009L2 — The pair is a system too\u0009Synopsis","header":"5.3.1.2. PKC vocabulary in scope","id":"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L2-___-The-pair-is-a-system-too--Synopsis--PKC-vocabulary-in-scope"}});